{"availability":"available","full":"twcclegg/libphonenumber-csharp","name":"libphonenumber-csharp","description":"Offical C# port of https://github.com/googlei18n/libphonenumber","category":"Other","language":"C#","stars":924,"forks":158,"created":"2015-08-15T23:46:33Z","updated":"2026-10-18T04:30:04Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["csharp","e164","java-source","libphonenumber","phone-number","phonenumbers"],"demo":"https://twcclegg.github.io/libphonenumber-csharp/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T09:17:23.736Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T09:17:23.736Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T09:17:23.736Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T01:08:42.795Z","stars":924,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-15T14:57:53.306Z","stars":924,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-18T09:17:23.736Z","stars":924,"forks":158}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The original Apache License 2.0 was preserved.","Try the interactive demo → — parse, format, validate, and find phone numbers in your browser. No install required; runs entirely via WebAssembly. Browse the API reference → — generated from this library's XML doc comments.","Phone number metadata is updated in the Google repo approximately every two weeks. This library is automatically updated by a scheduled github action to include the latest metadata, usually within a day. See Metadata updates for how that works and how to run it manually."],"features":["Parsing/formatting/validating phone numbers for all countries/regions of the world.","GetNumberType - gets the type of the number based on the number itself; able to distinguish Fixed-line, Mobile, Toll-free, Premium Rate, Shared Cost, VoIP and Personal Numbers (whenever feasible).","IsNumberMatch - gets a confidence level on whether two numbers could be the same.","GetExampleNumber/GetExampleNumberByType - provides valid example numbers for 218 countries/regions, with the option of specifying which type o